			"date": "2025-10-14T21:10:04.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> it's not possible - see <a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@vrugtehagel/115308994476955114\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">mastodon.social/@vrugtehagel/1</span><span class=\"invisible\">15308994476955114</span></a></p><p>If you want to have metadata for properties, you're probably best off wrapping them with a proxy and using a mechanism (like a prefix or named symbols) to look up the metadata without those properties being included in `Object.keys()` and whatnot.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
